==Russian==
[[File:Rooster-1.jpg|thumbnail|Петух (1)]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|пѣтухъ}} {{ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
{{affix|ru|петь|-ух}}, said to have been influenced by {{m|ru|Пе́тя}}, diminutive of {{m|ru|Пётр}}. Related to {{m|ru|петь||to sing}}. Compare {{m|ru|пе́вень}}, {{cog|uk|пі́вень}}, {{cog|be|пе́вень}}, {{cog|bg|пете́л}}, {{cog|mk|петел}}, {{cog|sh|pijétao}}, {{m|sh|pijévac}}, {{cog|sl|petêlin}}, {{m|sl|pẹ́təł}}. Compare also {{cog|pl|piać||to crow}}, which is cognate with {{m|ru|петь}}. Likewise {{noncog|la|cano|canere}} means both “to sing” and “to crow”.

